# Commits and PRs

- Messages focus on **why** the change happened; follow recent history style (`git log`)
- Prefer Conventional Commits if the repo/commitlint requires it (`feat:`, `fix:`, `chore:`, etc.)
- **Never** add `Co-Authored-By` trailers (Claude, Cursor, Copilot, AI, or variants) in commits or PR descriptions
- Do not attribute the change to a tool/agent in the title or body
- Do not commit secrets (`.env`, tokens, credentials)
- Only create a commit/PR when the user explicitly asks
